WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:07.140
&gt;&gt; Good afternoon all. So, today

00:00:07.141 --> 00:00:08.535
I'm here to speak about rather

00:00:08.536 --> 00:00:10.320
emotional and
a very serious aspect of

00:00:10.321 --> 00:00:12.955
ones life, which is death.

00:00:12.956 --> 00:00:21.495
So, we bring back dead people
to life. I was joking.

00:00:21.496 --> 00:00:24.160
Okay. So, firstly thanks a lot,

00:00:24.161 --> 00:00:26.860
the Microsoft and some other
ventures for having us here.

00:00:26.861 --> 00:00:29.770
It's really a privilege to
be part of this workshop.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:31.970
So, I'm Shruthi Reddy,

00:00:31.971 --> 00:00:33.780
the founder of
Anthyesti Foundation.

00:00:33.781 --> 00:00:36.150
For after having worked
for about 10 years

00:00:36.151 --> 00:00:38.720
behind the computer,
Java programming, coding,

00:00:38.721 --> 00:00:41.185
I decided to call
it quits and then

00:00:41.186 --> 00:00:42.785
my pension for social sector

00:00:42.786 --> 00:00:45.140
had made me jump into
this entrepreneurship.

00:00:45.141 --> 00:00:48.600
So the project Amrit,

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:50.340
what exactly does Amrit mean?

00:00:50.341 --> 00:00:51.585
Amrit means, Amrit is

00:00:51.586 --> 00:00:53.360
a Sanskrit word which
means immortal.

00:00:53.361 --> 00:00:55.050
So through this project we aim to

00:00:55.051 --> 00:00:56.660
say that every human being

00:00:56.661 --> 00:00:58.310
can become immortal only

00:00:58.311 --> 00:01:00.455
because he's got the chance
to live another life,

00:01:00.456 --> 00:01:02.644
that is through organ donations.

00:01:02.645 --> 00:01:06.450
So during my tenure that is
where I met Mr. [inaudible] .

00:01:06.451 --> 00:01:09.050
He's also very equally
passionate person

00:01:09.051 --> 00:01:11.390
about organ donation
and he comes with

00:01:11.391 --> 00:01:12.500
about 18 years of experience

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:14.270
in the pharmaceutical industry.

00:01:14.271 --> 00:01:16.685
So, looking at the statistics,

00:01:16.686 --> 00:01:19.835
can you all believe
that in India only

00:01:19.836 --> 00:01:24.630
0.08 per million population
actually donated organs?

00:01:24.631 --> 00:01:26.720
It's not even like one percent

00:01:26.721 --> 00:01:28.595
and looking at the
statistics over here,

00:01:28.596 --> 00:01:31.680
in 2014 only 0.84 percent

00:01:31.681 --> 00:01:33.320
of the road traffic accidents

00:01:33.321 --> 00:01:38.720
got connoted to organ donations,
2015, 2016, 2017.

00:01:38.721 --> 00:01:40.030
Yes, there is an improvement
but then there

00:01:40.031 --> 00:01:41.465
is very mild improvement.

00:01:41.466 --> 00:01:43.610
No wide road traffic accidents
are specifically

00:01:43.611 --> 00:01:45.800
of our interest because most of

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:46.580
these road traffic accidents

00:01:46.581 --> 00:01:47.660
actually result in
something known

00:01:47.661 --> 00:01:49.610
as brain debts and brain debts

00:01:49.611 --> 00:01:51.230
are the most cases wherein we

00:01:51.231 --> 00:01:54.639
can do lot of
solid organ transplants.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.255
Just have a look at
a 2018 requirements.

00:01:58.256 --> 00:02:00.965
Three lack kidney transplants,

00:02:00.966 --> 00:02:03.030
40,000 heart transplants and

00:02:03.031 --> 00:02:07.100
25,000 liver transplants and
it's a very sad state to

00:02:07.101 --> 00:02:09.515
say that out of this probably in

00:02:09.516 --> 00:02:11.420
kidney transplant
just about two percent

00:02:11.421 --> 00:02:13.549
will get their
kidneys transplanted.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:15.590
Here it is about 0.1 percent in

00:02:15.591 --> 00:02:19.060
cardiac and 0.2 percent
in liver transplants.

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:25.140
So we Antyesti Foundation
we're relatively new NGO.

00:02:25.141 --> 00:02:26.380
It's been about one-and-half

00:02:26.381 --> 00:02:28.160
year and we have been
working extensively

00:02:28.161 --> 00:02:30.430
at the colleges in
the corporate level trying to

00:02:30.431 --> 00:02:33.290
do campaigning about
what organ donation is,

00:02:33.291 --> 00:02:35.780
helping people remove the myth
about organ donation.

00:02:35.781 --> 00:02:37.340
So in the process we have

00:02:37.341 --> 00:02:39.090
collected about a
thousand plus pledges,

00:02:39.091 --> 00:02:42.305
impacted about 1200 plus
colleges and corporates

00:02:42.306 --> 00:02:43.640
and we're also successful in

00:02:43.641 --> 00:02:46.509
training 50-plus
transplant coordinators.

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:50.040
Now, talking about what
exactly are the problems,

00:02:50.041 --> 00:02:51.240
why do we have such

00:02:51.241 --> 00:02:53.495
abysmally low rates
of organ donation?

00:02:53.496 --> 00:02:57.155
Firstly is the public attitude
towards organ donation.

00:02:57.156 --> 00:02:59.840
So if you really go to
public and then you say that

00:02:59.841 --> 00:03:01.040
are you interested in doing

00:03:01.041 --> 00:03:03.055
organ donations
after a person dies?

00:03:03.056 --> 00:03:04.850
Speculatively, no
because they've got

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:06.720
so many myths about
organ donation.

00:03:06.721 --> 00:03:09.415
A person would say that oh
no if you take my eyes in

00:03:09.416 --> 00:03:12.940
this life probably I might
be born blind in next life.

00:03:12.941 --> 00:03:15.280
Yes, this is truth. This
is what people say to us.

00:03:15.281 --> 00:03:19.760
Then step two is coming about
consent for organ donation.

00:03:19.761 --> 00:03:22.080
So let me just explain
the meaning of organ donation.

00:03:22.081 --> 00:03:24.020
Organ donation is
a process wherein when

00:03:24.021 --> 00:03:26.000
a person is still alive with

00:03:26.001 --> 00:03:28.595
his own consent he
can get his organs

00:03:28.596 --> 00:03:31.580
to the needy or when
the person is not alive,

00:03:31.581 --> 00:03:32.800
he's dead, then
with the consent of

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:35.555
his relatives then he
can donate the organs.

00:03:35.556 --> 00:03:37.880
So step two where we
tackle is about we need

00:03:37.881 --> 00:03:40.325
to get consent of relatives
of organ donation.

00:03:40.326 --> 00:03:43.355
So let's say that I have
pledged for my organs and if

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:44.780
I die a brain-death but

00:03:44.781 --> 00:03:46.290
if my relatives
aren't aware of it,

00:03:46.291 --> 00:03:48.380
if my [inaudible] do not know
about it then the hospital

00:03:48.381 --> 00:03:50.875
cannot do anything to
harvest my organs.

00:03:50.876 --> 00:03:52.330
The next step is the

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:54.289
brain-death identification
and certification.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:56.810
So if you see this
there's actually

00:03:56.811 --> 00:03:57.875
a lot that goes into

00:03:57.876 --> 00:03:59.925
identifying brain-death
and certifying.

00:03:59.926 --> 00:04:01.760
In India the process
says that there are

00:04:01.761 --> 00:04:03.440
about four doctors from

00:04:03.441 --> 00:04:06.260
various backgrounds who have
to come at an interval of

00:04:06.261 --> 00:04:09.380
six hours each and then
identify the brain death.

00:04:09.381 --> 00:04:12.320
After this three major
hurdles are crossed,

00:04:12.321 --> 00:04:14.930
we are not yet game because there

00:04:14.931 --> 00:04:16.370
is lot more that comes

00:04:16.371 --> 00:04:17.960
from adequate hospital
infrastructure.

00:04:17.961 --> 00:04:19.565
So if the hospitals do not have

00:04:19.566 --> 00:04:23.360
a very good organ retrieval team
then it's a waste.

00:04:23.361 --> 00:04:24.770
After that, in spite of having

00:04:24.771 --> 00:04:26.120
a good organ retrieval team,

00:04:26.121 --> 00:04:27.950
we need to have got logistics for

00:04:27.951 --> 00:04:30.260
the transport of organs
to the recipient's body.

00:04:30.261 --> 00:04:32.400
So there were cases where
organs have actually traveled

00:04:32.401 --> 00:04:33.970
like thousand kilometers and

00:04:33.971 --> 00:04:36.245
they were fitted into
the recipient's body.

00:04:36.246 --> 00:04:37.880
This is what actually leads to

00:04:37.881 --> 00:04:39.860
a successful organ transplant.

00:04:39.861 --> 00:04:42.170
So, yes, each and
every point in this

00:04:42.171 --> 00:04:45.810
explains leads to one
successful organ transplant.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:49.100
So talking about
the first point, that is,

00:04:49.101 --> 00:04:51.260
how can AI machine
or learning actually

00:04:51.261 --> 00:04:53.930
implement an overall positive

00:04:53.931 --> 00:04:56.000
public attitude in
the general public?

00:04:56.001 --> 00:04:58.280
Because so far we've been
reaching out to colleges,

00:04:58.281 --> 00:05:00.650
corporates personally but
I think if you really

00:05:00.651 --> 00:05:06.115
implement the programs online
and leverage social media,

00:05:06.116 --> 00:05:07.435
for let say we are creating

00:05:07.436 --> 00:05:09.890
online recorded webinars
and which is going to

00:05:09.891 --> 00:05:11.900
the public etc and then we

00:05:11.901 --> 00:05:14.705
are able to record the pledges.

00:05:14.706 --> 00:05:17.295
Once we know
a particular pledgee,

00:05:17.296 --> 00:05:18.470
using Facebook data analytics

00:05:18.471 --> 00:05:19.430
probably we can get to know about

00:05:19.431 --> 00:05:22.640
the cultural preferences,
their dataset,

00:05:22.641 --> 00:05:25.850
their behavioral preferences
and in turn start using

00:05:25.851 --> 00:05:28.520
this customized audiences
marketing in order to market

00:05:28.521 --> 00:05:31.370
to the relatives and to
their total communities.

00:05:31.371 --> 00:05:32.810
So this is one place where we

00:05:32.811 --> 00:05:35.240
can possibly use social media to

00:05:35.241 --> 00:05:36.700
a lot extent for

00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:38.780
the mass awareness
campaigns which I

00:05:38.781 --> 00:05:40.025
guess nobody in India is doing

00:05:40.026 --> 00:05:41.435
regarding to organ donation.

00:05:41.436 --> 00:05:44.880
So can we convert pledge data
into real donations?

00:05:44.881 --> 00:05:46.850
Yes, this is one of
the major aspect how

00:05:46.851 --> 00:05:49.850
we can use social media
for doing it.

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:53.150
Now this is again
another startling fact.

00:05:53.151 --> 00:05:55.430
There are at least 10
to 12 patients who are

00:05:55.431 --> 00:05:58.125
admitted in ICU and are
declared brain-dead.

00:05:58.126 --> 00:06:00.410
So, can I have a show
of hands as to

00:06:00.411 --> 00:06:03.630
how many over here know
what a brain death is.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:07.875
Okay, that's like
just 10 percent.

00:06:07.876 --> 00:06:10.200
Okay, [inaudible] you want
to say about brain death?

00:06:10.201 --> 00:06:12.645
&gt;&gt; Yeah. First of all,

00:06:12.646 --> 00:06:19.470
I would just like to, thanks.

00:06:19.471 --> 00:06:22.280
Organ donation we need to be
a little bit more specific.

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:25.320
Here we are talking
about the solid organs.

00:06:25.321 --> 00:06:28.315
Solid organs means
the heart, the liver,

00:06:28.316 --> 00:06:30.260
the kidneys which are extremely

00:06:30.261 --> 00:06:33.240
vital to human being's life.

00:06:33.241 --> 00:06:35.060
There are certain tissue also

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:36.795
which fall into
this particular garment

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:40.605
of organ donation like the
cornea's, it's a tissue.

00:06:40.606 --> 00:06:43.140
Skin, it's a tissue.

00:06:43.141 --> 00:06:45.365
There are some stem
cell transplantations

00:06:45.366 --> 00:06:49.310
also which requires for
a hematopoietic patient.

00:06:49.311 --> 00:06:50.780
So there are different kinds

00:06:50.781 --> 00:06:52.505
of category of organ donation.

00:06:52.506 --> 00:06:55.580
Why I need clarity over here is

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:58.700
because solid organs
are something which

00:06:58.701 --> 00:07:01.955
a patient is in
the death bed waiting

00:07:01.956 --> 00:07:06.245
for the next day maybe
he will be alive or not.

00:07:06.246 --> 00:07:08.270
In a situation where

00:07:08.271 --> 00:07:10.100
the extreme amount of

00:07:10.101 --> 00:07:12.310
seriousness of
the patient is there,

00:07:12.311 --> 00:07:14.990
how many of us has
actually witnessed

00:07:14.991 --> 00:07:18.720
a patient who is in
dialysis for five years?

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:23.270
Now, every month
the patient goes to

00:07:23.271 --> 00:07:25.100
the hospital and the doctor only

00:07:25.101 --> 00:07:28.415
tells that you know
you were in stage 3A,

00:07:28.416 --> 00:07:30.505
now you're in stage 3B.

00:07:30.506 --> 00:07:32.530
So, some a technology,

00:07:32.531 --> 00:07:35.270
some medical information
has been incorporated.

00:07:35.271 --> 00:07:40.010
Some seriousness is being
propagated to the next level.

00:07:40.011 --> 00:07:42.680
So, organ donation and

00:07:42.681 --> 00:07:44.630
the solid organ donation
the seriousness

00:07:44.631 --> 00:07:46.300
and some kind of intelligence,

00:07:46.301 --> 00:07:48.865
if we can marry it,

00:07:48.866 --> 00:07:51.180
it becomes more meaningful.

00:07:51.181 --> 00:07:54.410
Second part,
the brainstem did part.

00:07:54.411 --> 00:07:57.975
The brain is majorly
of the cortex,

00:07:57.976 --> 00:08:00.010
but there is a stem also.

00:08:00.011 --> 00:08:02.065
Now, if for certain reason,

00:08:02.066 --> 00:08:04.665
the stem is not active,

00:08:04.666 --> 00:08:08.930
it is legally as per medically
it is a dead person.

00:08:08.931 --> 00:08:11.585
It is an irreversible death.

00:08:11.586 --> 00:08:16.600
A patient who's in a coma
is a reversible one.

00:08:16.601 --> 00:08:19.020
So, his stem is not dead.

00:08:19.021 --> 00:08:20.960
Maybe the other functions are

00:08:20.961 --> 00:08:23.540
not actually properly working,

00:08:23.541 --> 00:08:27.010
but the brainstem is
a clear cut case of death.

00:08:27.011 --> 00:08:28.910
Now, this awareness is

00:08:28.911 --> 00:08:31.460
mostly not there
with common people.

00:08:31.461 --> 00:08:34.140
I have been interacting
and very closely and

00:08:34.141 --> 00:08:36.800
working with a lot of doctors
of the medical fraternity.

00:08:36.801 --> 00:08:39.805
Especially the ideals as
well as the intensivist.

00:08:39.806 --> 00:08:43.480
Even they are a little bit
reluctant that no,

00:08:43.481 --> 00:08:45.395
I don't have this kind
of technology,

00:08:45.396 --> 00:08:47.130
which can really tell me that

00:08:47.131 --> 00:08:49.265
this patient is
totally brain-dead.

00:08:49.266 --> 00:08:52.380
Tomorrow, somebody will
catch hold of me and tell

00:08:52.381 --> 00:08:55.735
me what is the proof that
this patient was brain dead.

00:08:55.736 --> 00:08:57.600
So, there are certain things in

00:08:57.601 --> 00:08:59.800
medical record which
they practice.

00:08:59.801 --> 00:09:02.200
Every six hours as
[inaudible] told they

00:09:02.201 --> 00:09:05.135
check it with
a committee of doctors,

00:09:05.136 --> 00:09:08.260
in an unbiased way,
and finally sign.

00:09:08.261 --> 00:09:10.515
What are laundry list of

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:16.005
tests which confirms that
the patient is brainstem dead?

00:09:16.006 --> 00:09:18.570
&gt;&gt;So, yeah. So
actually a majority of

00:09:18.571 --> 00:09:20.810
road traffic accidents
lead to brainstem dead.

00:09:20.811 --> 00:09:22.420
So, in brain death
cases what people

00:09:22.421 --> 00:09:24.190
lose their discipline
put on a ventilator,

00:09:24.191 --> 00:09:26.800
and all the other organs are
actually kept ventilated.

00:09:26.801 --> 00:09:28.360
So, although the brain is dead,

00:09:28.361 --> 00:09:29.795
the other organs there is

00:09:29.796 --> 00:09:32.330
proper oxygen supply and
blood supplies there,

00:09:32.331 --> 00:09:35.380
and each organ has
got its own life to

00:09:35.381 --> 00:09:36.470
get transplanted like for example

00:09:36.471 --> 00:09:38.630
the heart at the max you
got four to six hours.

00:09:38.631 --> 00:09:40.220
So, between this
four to six hours,

00:09:40.221 --> 00:09:41.790
the organ needs to
be removed from

00:09:41.791 --> 00:09:43.720
the donor and put
into the recipient.

00:09:43.721 --> 00:09:45.050
That is crossing all those five

00:09:45.051 --> 00:09:46.515
or six levels whatever
I have explained.

00:09:46.516 --> 00:09:49.030
Kidneys are the maximum
can be held what

00:09:49.031 --> 00:09:52.045
24 hours to 48 hours for
kidney which is again,

00:09:52.046 --> 00:09:53.450
probably a sad state that kidney

00:09:53.451 --> 00:09:57.835
one-off organ that can be
removed from a living person.

00:09:57.836 --> 00:09:59.750
So, that is where
the trafficking happens.

00:09:59.751 --> 00:10:01.390
A lot of exploitation happens.

00:10:01.391 --> 00:10:02.630
Same with the liver as well.

00:10:02.631 --> 00:10:04.890
Liver and kidneys as well,
living donations happen.

00:10:04.891 --> 00:10:07.280
So, now coming to can we increase

00:10:07.281 --> 00:10:10.230
success rate of PAC declarations
into transplants?

00:10:10.231 --> 00:10:12.050
I think yes. Definitely, using

00:10:12.051 --> 00:10:14.585
technology and
mobile applications, yes.

00:10:14.586 --> 00:10:16.530
One such being notifications.

00:10:16.531 --> 00:10:18.990
So, what if our
brainstem dead donor

00:10:18.991 --> 00:10:20.600
is identified in an ICU?

00:10:20.601 --> 00:10:21.615
And, all people who were

00:10:21.616 --> 00:10:22.870
involved in the
stakeholder change,

00:10:22.871 --> 00:10:24.605
given notifications that there's

00:10:24.606 --> 00:10:27.035
possible brain-dead case,
come on now act.

00:10:27.036 --> 00:10:28.620
So, if you get into
what shooting at

00:10:28.621 --> 00:10:30.090
a mechanism and the status

00:10:30.091 --> 00:10:31.390
is being populated from state

00:10:31.391 --> 00:10:33.130
one to state two to state four,

00:10:33.131 --> 00:10:35.600
the complete time lag
whatever it is dead,

00:10:35.601 --> 00:10:38.370
from the harvesting
of the organ to

00:10:38.371 --> 00:10:40.310
putting the organ into
the recipient's body

00:10:40.311 --> 00:10:41.840
that is totally eliminated,

00:10:41.841 --> 00:10:43.625
and what the other advantage?

00:10:43.626 --> 00:10:45.405
Like if you want to
collect this data,

00:10:45.406 --> 00:10:47.730
any reason and give you
a couple of states which

00:10:47.731 --> 00:10:50.525
are having the
transplant waiting list.

00:10:50.526 --> 00:10:53.040
So, the more and more we
have successful transplant,

00:10:53.041 --> 00:10:55.465
the more and more they would
increase the prediction of,

00:10:55.466 --> 00:10:57.100
what kind of good news
will we match with

00:10:57.101 --> 00:10:59.005
what kind of patterns?

00:10:59.006 --> 00:11:02.925
Or who is possible recipient
of this kind of liver?

00:11:02.926 --> 00:11:05.380
Yeah, a guidebook and
the green channel.

00:11:05.381 --> 00:11:08.085
So generally,

00:11:08.086 --> 00:11:11.990
not all surgeons have
the ability to do transplants.

00:11:11.991 --> 00:11:13.250
So, there is
a specific guidebook,

00:11:13.251 --> 00:11:14.570
which is right now

00:11:14.571 --> 00:11:16.730
being spoken about by
the NGOs et cetera,

00:11:16.731 --> 00:11:18.710
who are already
doing a transplants.

00:11:18.711 --> 00:11:21.330
So, that can be also part
of the technology but,

00:11:21.331 --> 00:11:22.605
and the green channel.

00:11:22.606 --> 00:11:24.500
So, as I told that this there
is lots of logistics in

00:11:24.501 --> 00:11:26.600
world specifically in
the transport of organs.

00:11:26.601 --> 00:11:28.550
If the police et cetera,

00:11:28.551 --> 00:11:30.190
they already trained
